  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The bow tie – one-touch passing between four lines",
  "description": "Four lines in a rectangle, two on each side, with the first player in each line facing in. The ball goes round with one-touch passes in a bow-tie pattern: A passes diagonally to B, B straight up to C, C diagonally to D and D straight up to A. After passing, go to the back of your own line.\n\nVariations: pass forehand only, then backhand only, and send the ball the other way round. With many players: add a second ball. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Quick, accurate passes along the floor, without bounces."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Take a step towards the ball and play it first time."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Show with your stick where you want the ball."
    }
  ],
